why_now: Node filter had duplicate entries; filter only applied to PmItem nodes; version constant was outdated
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-10T20:52:36.642Z",claude-opus,"Follow-up fix during PR #19 verification: the same-key OR merge only worked on the export/shapeGraph path. The analytics path (explain/analyze/neighbors/cycles/path/impact) went through parseAnalyticsFlags, which called parseNodeFilter once PER --filter flag and concatenated results — so 'explain <id> --filter status=open --filter status=in_progress' produced two separate status entries that AND to an impossible condition, dropping the item (verified: item returned NOTFOUND despite matching). Fixed parseAnalyticsFlags to accumulate raw --filter terms and call parseNodeFilter once at the end; exported it and added a regression test. Also fixed the Greptile P1 release.yml bug (bash expanded $1 in the node -e EXTENSION_VERSION replacement, corrupting src to 'const \"<ver>\";' and breaking the release build) via a function replacement. Rebuilt, 55/55 tests pass, changelog check green, end-to-end explain OR filter now correct."
body: ""
